// REQUIRES: long
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-inst-work.py 16 1000 > %t.big.gopp
// RUN: not %gopp check %t.big.gopp > %t.check 2>&1
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.check
// RUN: grep -c 'error\[' %t.check | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONE
// RUN: not %gopp build -emit=gir %t.big.gopp > %t.build 2>&1
// RUN: diff %t.check %t.build
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-inst-work.py 9 1000 > %t.ok.gopp
// RUN: %gopp check %t.ok.gopp
// P04.08 (GEN-5), review R4: the code the instances of a package hold is
// bounded, not only their number. The walk visits at most 4000000 nodes of
// code (LowerOptions::MaxWalkedNodes), or 16 per byte of the source if that
// is more; past it is one error, the same text from `gopp check` and the
// build (the walk is one, in one order), and no more instances, so a
// 20 KB file of 2^15 instances of a 1000-statement body (about 230 million
// nodes) stops at once instead of filling the memory. The other side: 2^8
// instances of the body (about 1.8 million nodes) check. Long: the walk
// visits 4 million nodes first (under a second, more under ASan). The fast
// side is the unit test GIRInstances.TheWorkBudgetIsOneErrorAndStopsTheWalk.
// (One error is counted with grep, not --implicit-check-not, so that
// sema/exact-errors.test, which reruns such commands, leaves this long input
// to check-long.)
// CHECK: big.gopp:81:16: error[E0449]: cannot instantiate F0: the instances of the package hold more than 4000000 nodes of code (GEN-5)
// CHECK: note: instantiated from F0[
// CHECK: note: ... and 13 more instantiations
// ONE: {{^}}1{{$}}
